\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the above by writing $C=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K$ for another arbitrary constant $K,$ and then we can combine the two terms using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡K) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|2x+3|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we finally conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|2x+3|).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c42be74-d37e-575a-90eb-169916a58b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3x+4|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244993} {:answer/id #uuid "7c954e85-2e68-534c-8bde-f7437515282b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3x+4|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245405} {:answer/id #uuid "9b15fd0c-a519-5e0e-babc-d7581f89c710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{|3x+4|}{K})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245683} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a569fc-8916-5c83-804a-2f6bb67e096b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3x+4|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245821} {:answer/id #uuid "dc610f8a-7443-5fdc-957b-12a2841d674a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3x+4|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc610f8a-7443-5fdc-957b-12a2841d674a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|3x+4|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246271} :answer-field/id #uuid "62cdbf79-0576-5391-870b-ffe8fe9a5e07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/iden